# Consolidated C++26 & Feature Fixes - BertieBot

## Executive Summary

Four agents assessed core, v0.5.0, mechanisms, and build system. Key issues:

1. **No-op implementations** - Many functions return true/void without doing real work
2. **Missing libpq** - No PostgreSQL integration in core
3. **C++26 gaps** - Not using std::expected, RAII wrappers, std::ranges consistently
4. **Build issues** - Macro mismatches, .hpp files as sources, excluded features

---

## Critical Fixes Needed

### 1. Fix Macro Mismatches (CRITICAL)

**Issue:** `HAVE_POSTGRESQL` vs `HAS_POSTGRESQL` causing destructor to never clean up

**Files to Fix:**
- `v0.4.1/executable_mechanisms/file_absorber.cpp` - Destructor uses wrong macro

**Fix:**
```cpp
// Unify on BERTIEBOT_HAVE_LIBPQ
#ifdef BERTIEBOT_HAVE_LIBPQ
    PQfinish(db_);
#endif
```

### 2. Remove .hpp from Executable Sources (CRITICAL)

**Issue:** `suggestions_mechanism.hpp` listed as source for bridge_server

**File:** `v0.4.1/CMakeLists.txt`

**Fix:** Remove .hpp from add_executable(), keep only .cpp files

### 3. Implement RAII Wrappers for PostgreSQL (HIGH)

**New File:** `v0.5.0/core/raii_pgconnection.hpp`

```cpp
#pragma once
#include <memory>
#include <libpq-fe.h>

namespace BertieBot {
namespace DB {

struct PGConnDeleter {
    void operator()(PGconn* conn) const {
        if (conn) PQfinish(conn);
    }
};

using PGConnPtr = std::unique_ptr<PGconn, PGConnDeleter>;

class PGConnection {
public:
    explicit PGConnection(const std::string& conninfo);
    ~PGConnection() = default;

    // Move only
    PGConnection(PGConnection&&) = default;
    PGConnection& operator=(PGConnection&&) = default;
    PGConnection(const PGConnection&) = delete;
    PGConnection& operator=(const PGConnection&) = delete;

    [[nodiscard]] bool is_connected() const;
    [[nodiscard]] PGconn* raw() const { return conn_.get(); }

    // C++26: Use std::expected for error handling
    [[nodiscard]] std::expected<PGresult*, std::string> 
    query(const std::string& sql);

private:
    PGConnPtr conn_;
};

} // namespace DB
} // namespace BertieBot
```

### 4. Add std::expected Polyfill (HIGH)

**New File:** `v0.5.0/include/bertiebot/expected.hpp`

```cpp
#pragma once
#include <version>

#ifdef __cpp_lib_expected
    #include <expected>
    namespace BertieBot {
        template<typename T, typename E>
        using expected = std::expected<T, E>;
        using std::unexpected;
    }
#else
    // Polyfill for C++20/23
    #include <variant>
    #include <utility>

    namespace BertieBot {

    template<typename T, typename E>
    class expected {
        std::variant<T, E> data_;
        bool has_value_;

    public:
        expected(T value) : data_(std::move(value)), has_value_(true) {}
        expected(E error) : data_(std::move(error)), has_value_(false) {}

        [[nodiscard]] bool has_value() const { return has_value_; }
        [[nodiscard]] T& value() { return std::get<T>(data_); }
        [[nodiscard]] const T& value() const { return std::get<T>(data_); }
        [[nodiscard]] E& error() { return std::get<E>(data_); }
        [[nodiscard]] const E& error() const { return std::get<E>(data_); }

        T& operator*() { return value(); }
        const T& operator*() const { return value(); }
        T* operator->() { return &value(); }
    };

    template<typename E>
    class unexpected {
        E error_;
    public:
        explicit unexpected(E e) : error_(std::move(e)) {}
        E& value() { return error_; }
    };

    } // namespace BertieBot
#endif
```

### 5. Fix Audit Mechanism Header/CPP Mismatch (HIGH)

**Files:**
- `v0.4.1/executable_mechanisms/audit_mechanism.hpp`
- `v0.4.1/executable_mechanisms/audit_mechanism.cpp`

**Fix:** Align member variable names:
```cpp
// In .hpp:
std::unique_ptr<DB::PGConnection> db_connection;
std::unique_ptr<LamiaBridge> lamia_bridge;

// In .cpp - use same names, not db_connection_ptr
```

### 6. Use std::scoped_lock (MEDIUM)

**Replace in all files:**
```cpp
// BEFORE:
std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mutex_);

// AFTER (C++26):
std::scoped_lock lock(mutex_);  // Handles multiple mutexes, cleaner
```

### 7. Use std::ranges (MEDIUM)

**Example in absorber/exporter:**
```cpp
// BEFORE:
for (const auto& file : files) {
    if (should_process(file)) {
        process(file);
    }
}

// AFTER (C++20/26):
namespace rv = std::ranges::views;
auto files_to_process = files 
    | rv::filter(&should_process)
    | rv::take(100);

std::ranges::for_each(files_to_process, &process);
```

### 8. Fix Signal Handler (MEDIUM)

**File:** Various main.cpp files

```cpp
// BEFORE (bad):
void signal_handler(int) { exit(0); }

// AFTER (good):
std::atomic<bool> g_running{true};
void signal_handler(int) { 
    g_running = false; 
}

int main() {
    // ... setup ...
    while (g_running) {
        // main loop
    }
    // cleanup
    return 0;
}
```

### 9. Add PostgreSQL to v0.4.1 CMake (HIGH)

**File:** `v0.4.1/CMakeLists.txt`

```cmake
# Add near top:
find_package(PostgreSQL QUIET)
if(PostgreSQL_FOUND)
    add_compile_definitions(BERTIEBOT_HAVE_LIBPQ=1)
    include_directories(${PostgreSQL_INCLUDE_DIRS})
endif()

# Link to targets that need it:
target_link_libraries(bertiebot_server PRIVATE
    $<$<BOOL:${PostgreSQL_FOUND}>:${PostgreSQL_LIBRARIES}>
)
```

### 10. Document No-Op Functions (LOW)

Add to each stub function:
```cpp
// TODO(BertieBot): Implement actual database query
// Currently returns empty result to allow compilation
[[deprecated("Not yet implemented - returns empty results")]]
std::vector<AuditEntry> QueryAudits(const std::string& pfql_query);
```

