# Dual-Stack Integration Usage

## Overview

The dual-stack integration connects MedusaServ, PsiForceDB, and K-Means XML catalog systems.

## Components

### 1. DualStackIPManager
- Manages IPv4/IPv6 binding
- Network interface detection
- IP configuration

### 2. MedusaServPsiForceDBIntegration
- Routes HTTP requests to appropriate systems
- Handles K-Means XML catalog requests
- Handles PsiForceDB requests
- Handles Lamia execution requests

## Usage

### Initialization

```cpp
#include "dual_stack_integration.h"

using namespace PsiForceDB::Integration;

// Create integration instance
MedusaServPsiForceDBIntegration integration;

// Initialize with components
integration.Initialize(
    medusaserv_processor,  // MedusaServ RequestProcessor*
    kmeans_manager,        // KMeansXMLCatalogManager*
    "psiforcedb://connection_string"
);
```

### Handling Requests

```cpp
// In request handler
MedusaServ::Network::ServerEngine::HttpRequest request;
MedusaServ::Network::ServerEngine::HttpResponse response;

if (integration.HandleIntegratedRequest(request, response)) {
    // Request was handled by integration
    // Send response
} else {
    // Let MedusaServ handle it normally
}
```

### Configuration

```cpp
UnifiedServerConfig config;
config.port = 80;
config.bind_address = "0.0.0.0";
config.enable_lamia_execution = true;
config.enable_psiforcedb_routing = true;
config.enable_kmeans_routing = true;

// Configure IP
config.ip_config.port = 80;
config.ip_config.bind_address = "0.0.0.0";
config.ip_config.enable_ipv4 = true;

ConfigureUnifiedServer(config, integration);
```

