## 🔍 Parsing and Analysis

### Tokenization Process

The parsing process begins with tokenization, where the raw query string is broken down into meaningful tokens for further processing.

```
Input: "pf://db::select; users --where="age > 25" --limit=10"

Tokenization:
├── PROTOCOL: "pf://"
├── NAMESPACE: "db"
├── COMMAND: "select"
├── TERMINATOR: ";"
├── ARGUMENT: "users"
├── OPTION: "--where="age > 25""
└── OPTION: "--limit=10"
```

### Abstract Syntax Tree (AST) Generation

The parser generates an AST that represents the logical structure of the query for optimization and execution.

```
AST Structure:
QueryNode
├── Protocol: "pf"
├── Namespace: "db"
├── Command: "select"
├── Arguments: ["users"]
└── Options:
    ├── where: "age > 25"
    └── limit: "10"
```

### Semantic Analysis

After parsing, semantic analysis validates the query against the database schema and resolves references.

#### Schema Validation
```cpp
class SchemaValidator {
public:
    ValidationResult validate(const ASTNode& ast) {
        // Validate table existence
        if (!tableExists(ast.getTableName())) {
            return ValidationResult::error("Table does not exist");
        }

        // Validate column references
        for (const auto& column : ast.getColumns()) {
            if (!columnExists(ast.getTableName(), column)) {
