## 🚀 Execution Engine

### Parallel Execution Architecture

The execution engine supports parallel processing to maximize throughput and minimize latency.

#### Thread Pool Management
```cpp
class QueryThreadPool {
private:
    std::vector<std::thread> workers;
    ThreadSafeQueue<Task> taskQueue;
    std::atomic<bool> shutdownFlag{false};

public:
    void submitTask(const Task& task) {
        taskQueue.push(task);
    }

    void executePlan(const ExecutionPlan& plan) {
        // Break plan into parallelizable tasks
        auto tasks = plan.generateParallelTasks();

        // Submit tasks to thread pool
        for (const auto& task : tasks) {
            submitTask(task);
        }

        // Wait for completion
        waitForCompletion(tasks);
    }
};
```

#### Memory Management
```cpp
class QueryMemoryManager {
private:
    MemoryPool pool;
    std::unordered_map<QueryId, MemoryContext> contexts;

public:
    MemoryContext allocateContext(const QueryId& queryId, size_t size) {
        auto context = pool.allocate(size);
        contexts[queryId] = context;
        return context;
    }

    void releaseContext(const QueryId& queryId) {
        auto it = contexts.find(queryId);
        if (it != contexts.end()) {
            pool.deallocate(it->second);
            contexts.erase(it);
        }
    }
};
```

