# Security Best Practices Guide

## 🛡️ Comprehensive Security Guidelines for PsiForceDB

This guide provides essential security best practices for deploying, configuring, and operating PsiForceDB in production environments. Following these guidelines will help ensure your database systems maintain the highest levels of security and compliance.

## 📋 Security Framework Overview

### Zero Trust Architecture
PsiForceDB implements a Zero Trust security model where every interaction is verified and validated, regardless of origin or previous authentication status.

### Defense in Depth
Multiple layers of security controls are implemented throughout the system to provide redundancy and ensure that the compromise of one layer does not lead to system-wide vulnerability.

### Proactive Security
Rather than simply reacting to threats, PsiForceDB actively anticipates and prevents attacks using AI-powered threat intelligence and behavioral analysis.

