# LFSSL Swappable Module Architecture

## Philosophy
**"Everything uses OpenSSL BUT it depends which book you read"**

The foundation provides **interfaces**, not implementations.
Modules can be swapped in/out as technology evolves.

## Architecture

```
LFSSL Core (Foundation)
├── Interfaces (Abstract - Never Change)
│   ├── ICryptoProvider
│   ├── ITLSProvider
│   ├── IHashProvider
│   └── IKeyExchangeProvider
│
└── Implementations (Swappable Modules)
    ├── OpenSSL Module (Current)
    ├── Native Module (Our Implementation)
    ├── BoringSSL Module (Alternative)
    ├── LibreSSL Module (Alternative)
    └── Hardware Module (Future)
```

## Module Interface Pattern

### Example: Crypto Provider Interface
```cpp
namespace LFSSL {
namespace Core {

// INTERFACE (Immutable Foundation)
class ICryptoProvider {
public:
    virtual ~ICryptoProvider() = default;

    // Hash functions
    virtual std::vector<uint8_t> sha256(const uint8_t* data, size_t len) = 0;
    virtual std::vector<uint8_t> sha384(const uint8_t* data, size_t len) = 0;
    virtual std::vector<uint8_t> sha512(const uint8_t* data, size_t len) = 0;

    // AES functions
    virtual std::vector<uint8_t> aes256_encrypt(
        const uint8_t* key, const uint8_t* iv,
        const uint8_t* plaintext, size_t len) = 0;

    // Key exchange
    virtual bool generate_keypair(...) = 0;

    // Module info
    virtual const char* getName() const = 0;
    virtual const char* getVersion() const = 0;
    virtual uint32_t getCapabilities() const = 0;
};

} // namespace Core
} // namespace LFSSL
```

