# PsiForceDB Nemadic Security System

## Overview

The Nemadic Security System provides seamless encryption/decryption and on-the-fly redaction for the PsiForceDB Nemadic framework. The system ensures that:

- **Automatic Decryption**: Bond payloads are decrypted automatically when loaded (if user has key)
- **On-the-fly Redaction**: Sensitive fields are redacted in real-time based on user permissions
- **Classification-Based Access**: Data classification (PUBLIC, INTERNAL, CONFIDENTIAL, SECRET) controls access
- **GDPR Compliance**: PII consent tracking and automatic redaction
- **2FA Integration**: Email 2FA trigger for SECRET-level data access
- **Complete Audit Trail**: All decryption/redaction actions are logged

## Architecture

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    NemadicSecureLoader                          │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  ┌──────────────┐  ┌──────────────┐  ┌──────────────┐          │
│  │   JWT Auth   │->│  Decryption  │->│  Redaction   │          │
│  │   & Perms    │  │ (AES-256-GCM)│  │   Engine     │          │
│  └──────────────┘  └──────────────┘  └──────────────┘          │
│         │                 │                 │                   │
│         v                 v                 v                   │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │
│  │                  SecureLoadResult                        │   │
│  │  (Decrypted + Redacted data ready for user)             │   │
│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## Components

### 1. NemadicSecurityContext (`nemadic_security_context.hpp`)

Manages user security context including:
- JWT session validation
- Clearance levels (UNCLASSIFIED → TOP_SECRET)
- Permission checking with caching
- 2FA state tracking
- GDPR consent management

```cpp
// Create security context from JWT
auto& validator = JWTSessionValidator::getInstance();
auto& context = SecurityContextManager::instance().create_context(session_id);

if (!context.initialize_from_jwt(jwt_token, validator)) {
    // Handle authentication failure
}

// Check clearance
can_access = context.can_access(ClassificationLevel::CONFIDENTIAL);

// Check permissions
has_read = context.has_permission("bond.read");

// 2FA management
if (context.requires_2fa_for(ClassificationLevel::SECRET)) {
    if (!context.is_2fa_valid()) {
        // Trigger 2FA challenge
        context.mark_2fa_verified("email");
    }
}
```

### 2. NemadicCrypto (`nemadic_crypto.hpp`)

Provides encryption/decryption with:
- AES-256-GCM encryption at rest
- Argon2id key derivation with hardware binding
- Per-bond unique keys derived from master key
- Secure memory management (locked RAM)

```cpp
// Initialize crypto
std::array<uint8_t, 32> master_key = /* load from secure storage */;
NemadicCryptoManager::instance().initialize(master_key);

// Encrypt bond payload
auto crypto = NemadicCryptoManager::instance().crypto();
auto payload = crypto.encrypt(
    bond_id,
    plaintext_data,
    ClassificationLevel::CONFIDENTIAL
);

// Attach to bond
crypto.attach_to_bond(bond, payload);

// Decrypt (with automatic permission check)
auto decrypted = crypto.decrypt_bond(bond, security_context);
```

### 3. RedactionEngine (`redaction_engine.hpp`)

Provides on-the-fly redaction with:
- Field-level redaction patterns
- Policy-based classification
- GDPR-sensitive field detection
- Automatic partial redaction (e.g., ***-**-1234 for SSN)

```cpp
// Create redaction engine
RedactionEngine engine;
engine.set_default_policy(RedactionPolicies::gdpr_policy());

// Redact JSON data
RedactionContext ctx{security_context, nullptr, "bond_123", "read"};
json redacted = engine.redact_json(json_data, ctx);

// Redact bond payload
DecryptedPayload payload = /* decrypted data */;
engine.redact_bond_payload(payload, bond, security_context);
```

### 4. NemadicSecureLoader (`nemadic_security_integration.hpp`)

The main integration point providing seamless operation:

```cpp
// Create secure loader for user
auto loader = NemadicSecureLoader::create(security_context);

// Load bond - handles decryption, 2FA, and redaction automatically
auto result = loader.load_bond(bond);

if (result.success) {
    // Access redacted data
    std::string data = result.as_string();
    json json_data = result.as_json();

    // Check what was redacted
    for (const auto& field : result.redacted_fields) {
        std::cout << "Field '" << field << "' was redacted\n";
    }
}
```

## Data Classification Levels

| Level | Clearance Required | Redaction Token | 2FA Required |
|-------|-------------------|-----------------|--------------|
| PUBLIC | UNCLASSIFIED | (none) | No |
| INTERNAL | RESTRICTED | [RESTRICTED] | No |
| CONFIDENTIAL | CONFIDENTIAL | [REDACTED] | Optional |
| RESTRICTED | SECRET | [CLASSIFIED] | Yes |
| SECRET | TOP_SECRET | [NO ACCESS] | Yes |
| CRITICAL | TOP_SECRET | [NO ACCESS] | Yes |

