# Differentially Private Order-Preserving Encryption (DP-OPE) Implementation

## Overview

This implementation provides **frequency-hiding Order-Preserving Encryption with differential privacy** for PsiForceDB. It protects against histogram attacks on sensitive fields (salary, age, dates) while preserving the ability to perform range queries on encrypted data.

## Features

### 1. Hypergeometric Distribution Noise (Frequency Hiding)
- Samples from hypergeometric distribution using crypto-secure random number generation
- Hides frequency information by adding probabilistic noise to ciphertexts
- Ensures identical plaintexts produce different ciphertexts (with high probability)
- Parameters: population size (N), success states (K), sample size (n)

### 2. Differential Privacy Laplace Noise
- Adds calibrated Laplace noise to range queries
- Provides formal differential privacy guarantees
- Privacy budget (epsilon) tracking per query
- Noise scale = sensitivity / epsilon

### 3. Privacy Budget Tracker
- Tracks privacy budget consumption across queries
- Implements standard differential privacy accounting
- Automatic budget reset at configurable intervals
- Query rejection when budget is exhausted

## Architecture

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    DP-OPE Cipher (DpOpeCipher)                  │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                                 │
│  ┌─────────────────┐  ┌──────────────────┐  ┌────────────────┐ │
│  │ Hypergeometric  │  │ Laplace Noise    │  │ Privacy Budget │ │
│  │ Sampler         │  │ Generator        │  │ Tracker        │ │
│  └────────┬────────┘  └────────┬─────────┘  └───────┬────────┘ │
│           │                    │                     │          │
│           ▼                    ▼                     ▼          │
│  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │
│  │         Frequency-Hiding Ciphertext Generator             │ │
│  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │
│                              │                                   │
│                              ▼                                   │
│  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │
│  │           OrderPreservingEncryption (Base OPE)            │ │
│  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │
│                                                                 │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## API Reference

### Main Classes

#### `DpOpeCipher`
Main class combining frequency-hiding OPE with differential privacy.

```cpp
// Configuration
struct Config {
    uint32_t plaintext_bits = 32;
    uint32_t ciphertext_bits = 64;
    HypergeometricSampler::Parameters hypergeom_params;
    LaplaceNoiseGenerator::Parameters laplace_params;
    PrivacyBudgetTracker::BudgetConfig budget_config;
    bool enable_frequency_hiding = true;
    bool enable_dp_noise = true;
};

// Construction
DpOpeCipher cipher(key, config);

// Encryption
auto ct = cipher.encrypt_int64(50000);      // Encrypt salary
auto ct = cipher.encrypt_double(25.5, 0, 100);  // Encrypt age

// Decryption (approximate)
int64_t approx = cipher.decrypt_approximate(ct);
auto range = cipher.decrypt_to_range(ct);   // Returns [min, max]

// Range queries with DP
auto result = cipher.generate_range_query(40000, 60000, 0.1);
// result.min_cipher, result.max_cipher, result.epsilon_consumed

// Count queries with DP
double noisy_count = cipher.query_with_noise(true_count, 0.1);

// Privacy budget
bool can_query = cipher.has_privacy_budget(0.1);
double remaining = cipher.get_remaining_budget();
```

#### `HypergeometricSampler`
Crypto-secure hypergeometric distribution sampler.

```cpp
HypergeometricSampler::Parameters params;
params.N = 1000;  // Population size
params.K = 100;   // Success states
params.n = 50;    // Sample size

HypergeometricSampler sampler(params);
uint64_t sample = sampler.sample_secure();  // Secure sampling
double mean = sampler.mean();               // Expected value
double var = sampler.variance();            // Variance
```

#### `LaplaceNoiseGenerator`
Differential privacy noise generator.

```cpp
LaplaceNoiseGenerator::Parameters params;
params.epsilon = 1.0;      // Privacy parameter
params.sensitivity = 1.0;  // Query sensitivity
params.compute_scale();    // Compute scale = sensitivity / epsilon

LaplaceNoiseGenerator generator(params);
double noise = generator.generate_noise();     // Generate noise
double noisy = generator.add_noise(value);     // Add noise to value
```

#### `PrivacyBudgetTracker`
Tracks privacy budget consumption.

```cpp
PrivacyBudgetTracker::BudgetConfig config;
config.total_epsilon = 1.0;           // Total privacy budget
config.reset_interval = std::chrono::hours(24);

PrivacyBudgetTracker tracker(config);
bool ok = tracker.consume_budget(0.1, "range_query");
double remaining = tracker.get_remaining_epsilon();
```

