## Feature Deep Dive

### 1. Searchable Encryption

**Problem:** How to search encrypted data without decrypting everything?

**Solution:** Multi-scheme encryption

```cpp
// Field-level encryption with scheme selection
class FieldLevelEncryption {
    // Deterministic: Same plaintext = same ciphertext
    // Use for: Exact match queries (=, IN, JOIN)
    std::vector<uint8_t> encrypt_deterministic(
        const std::string& plaintext,
        const EncryptionKey& key
    );

    // Order-Preserving: If a < b, then E(a) < E(b)
    // Use for: Range queries (BETWEEN, <, >)
    std::vector<uint8_t> encrypt_ope(
        const std::string& plaintext,
        const EncryptionKey& key
    );

    // Probabilistic: Same plaintext = different ciphertext
    // Use for: Maximum security, no search needed
    std::vector<uint8_t> encrypt_probabilistic(
        const std::string& plaintext,
        const EncryptionKey& key,
        const IV& iv
    );
};
```

**Query Example:**
```bash
# User searches for email
> find email=john@example.com

# System internally:
# 1. Classify field: EMAIL (use deterministic encryption)
# 2. Generate search token: HMAC(key, "john@example.com")
# 3. Query index: Find records with matching token
# 4. Result: Entity #456 matches
# 5. NO full decryption of other 10,000 records
```

### 2. Partial Decryption

**Problem:** Don't decrypt fields user doesn't need.

**Solution:** Metadata-only decryption for filtering

```cpp
class PartialDecryptionEngine {
    // Decrypt only fields specified in query
    NemadicEntity decrypt_selective(
        const EncryptedEntity& encrypted,
        const std::vector<std::string>& fields_to_decrypt,
        const JWTSession& session
    ) {
        NemadicEntity result;

        for (const auto& field : fields_to_decrypt) {
            if (can_decrypt(field, session)) {
                result[field] = decrypt_field(encrypted[field], session.key);
            } else {
                result[field] = RedactionMarker::INSUFFICIENT_CLEARANCE;
            }
        }

        // Keep other fields encrypted
        return result;
    }
};
```

### 3. Auto-Redaction

**Problem:** GDPR requires different users see different data.

**Solution:** Automatic redaction based on JWT clearance

```cpp
class AutoRedactionEngine {
    std::string redact_field(
        const std::string& value,
        DataType type,
        ClearanceLevel viewer_clearance
    ) {
        switch (type) {
            case DataType::EMAIL:
                if (viewer_clearance >= Clearance::CONFIDENTIAL) {
                    return mask_email(value);  // jo***@***.com
                } else {
                    return RedactionMarker::FULL;  // [REDACTED]
                }

            case DataType::SSN:
                if (viewer_clearance >= Clearance::SECRET) {
                    return mask_ssn(value);  // ***-**-6789
                } else {
                    return RedactionMarker::FULL;
                }

            case DataType::PHONE:
                return mask_phone(value);  // (***) ***-1234
        }
    }
};
```

### 4. Email TFA

**Problem:** Sensitive data needs extra protection.

**Solution:** Time-based 6-digit codes via email

```cpp
class EmailTFAProvider {
    TFAChallenge initiate_challenge(
        UserId user_id,
        OperationType operation,
        SensitivityLevel data_sensitivity
    ) {
        // Generate 6-digit code
        std::string code = generate_secure_code(6);

        // Hash with Argon2 (slow to prevent brute force)
        std::string code_hash = argon2_hash(code);

        // Send email
        send_email(
            user.email,
            "PsiForceDB Security Challenge",
            "Your verification code: " + code + "\nValid for 5 minutes."
        );

        return TFAChallenge{
            .user_id = user_id,
            .code_hash = code_hash,
            .expiry = now() + 300s,
            .attempts_remaining = 3
        };
    }

    bool verify_code(UserId user_id, const std::string& code) {
        auto challenge = get_challenge(user_id);

        if (challenge.expiry < now()) return false;  // Expired
        if (challenge.attempts_remaining == 0) return false;  // Locked

        if (argon2_verify(challenge.code_hash, code)) {
            mark_verified(user_id);
            return true;
        } else {
            challenge.attempts_remaining--;
            return false;
        }
    }
};
```

### 5. Audit Trail with Blockchain Integrity

**Problem:** Audit logs can be tampered with.

**Solution:** Hash chain linking every entry

```cpp
class AuditChain {
    struct AuditEntry {
        uint64_t sequence_number;
        std::string previous_hash;  // Hash of previous entry
        std::string data_hash;      // Hash of this entry's data
        std::vector<uint8_t> data;  // Encrypted audit data
    };

    // Verify chain hasn't been tampered
    VerificationResult verify_chain() {
        for (size_t i = 1; i < entries.size(); i++) {
            // Each entry's previous_hash must match previous entry's hash
            if (entries[i].previous_hash != hash(entries[i-1])) {
                return {false, i, "Chain broken at entry " + std::to_string(i)};
            }
        }
        return {true, 0, "Chain valid"};
    }
};
```

