## Security Analysis

### Attack Vectors Mitigated

| Attack | Layer Blocked | Mitigation |
|--------|---------------|------------|
| **Database Theft** | Encryption | All data encrypted at rest with AES-256-GCM |
| **Query Analysis** | Searchable Encryption | Deterministic/OPE schemes allow queries without revealing plaintext patterns |
| **Privilege Escalation** | Auto-Redaction | JWT clearance checked on every field access |
| **Session Hijacking** | TFA | Email 6-digit codes required for sensitive ops |
| **Audit Tampering** | Blockchain Chain | BLAKE3 hash chain links all entries |
| **Insider Threat** | Partial Decryption | Users only decrypt fields they need |
| **GDPR Violation** | Auto-Redaction | Automatic consent checking and redaction |
| **Replay Attack** | Error Context | Each command has unique timestamp + nonce |
| **Side-Channel** | Constant Time | Crypto operations use constant-time algorithms |

### Compliance Mapping

| Requirement | Implementation |
|-------------|----------------|
| **GDPR Article 17 (Right to Erasure)** | `data.erase` command with cascade deletion + audit |
| **GDPR Article 15 (Right to Access)** | `data.audit` with full history export |
| **GDPR Article 32 (Security)** | AES-256-GCM + Argon2 + hardware binding |
| **GDPR Article 5 (Accuracy)** | Diff logging tracks all corrections |
| **SOX (Audit Trail)** | Blockchain-integrity audit chain |
| **HIPAA (Access Control)** | Field-level redaction + TFA |
| **PCI-DSS (Encryption)** | Field-level encryption for card data |

